{"title":"Get Smart","description":"Forget the underlying plot in Get Smart, the modern-day cinematic adaptation of the classic TV series. What passes for one -- something about evil organization KAOS' attempts to bomb Los Angeles, with a preamble about weapons theft in Russia -- is rudimentary at best and confounding at worst. The movie is really the triumph-of-the-underdog story of Maxwell Smart (Steve Carell), a brilliant-but-nerdy analyst at secret government agency Control who finally gets his wish to become a field agent when headquarters is attacked and the identity of all of Control's operatives -- except for Agent 99 (Anne Hathaway) -- is compromised. It's up to Max and 99 to stop the bad guys and save the day ... provided they can learn to work together.","genres":["Comedy","Adventure","Action"]}],"info":[{"title":"Information","items":[{"title":"Studio","info":"Warner Bros."},{"title":"Released","info":"2008"},{"title":"Run Time","info":"1 hr 49 min"},{"title":"Rated","info":"PG-13 for some rude humor, action violence and language."},{"title":"Content Advisories","info":"Violence, Language, Sexual Content"},{"title":"Region of Origin","info":"United States"},{"title":null,"info":"© 2008 Warner Bros. Entertainment Inc."}]},{"title":"Languages","items":[{"title":"Original Audio","info":"English, English (United Kingdom)"},{"title":"Audio","info":"English (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC), Spanish (Latin America) (⁨Dolby 5.1⁩, AAC)"},{"title":"Subtitles","info":"English (CC), Spanish (Latin America) "}]},{"title":"Accessibility","items":[{"title":"(cc)","info":"Closed captions (CC) refer to subtitles in the available language with the addition of relevant non-dialogue information."}]}]}